          "maxLength": 255,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "start": {
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
  },
  {
    "description": "Confirm a prepared appointment after the caller explicitly said yes to the readback. A clear go-ahead such as "book it", "go ahead", "do it", "sounds good", "dale" or "adelante" is a yes; a question, a hedge ("wait", "maybe") or a change ("but at 2") is not. Only say it is booked once this returns ok. Retrying with the same token is safe. On CONFLICT the hold was lost: say so and offer the alternatives.",
    "name": "scheduling_book_commit",
    "parameters": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "confirmationToken": {
          "format": "uuid",
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "confirmationToken",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
  },
  {
    "description": "Prepare a message, callback request, complaint, quote request or intake for the business. Read the returned readback to the caller word for word and commit only after an explicit yes. For a message or callback, the callback number comes from caller ID when there is one; do not ask for it. On SLOT_MISSING, ask the caller the one question in callerSafeMessage and call prepare again; if the caller will not give a callback number, call prepare again without one and the message is filed without it. If exit is set, do not ask again: say callerSafeMessage.",
    "name": "tickets_open_prepare",
    "parameters": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
